        "PMC12005821::web::008::optimization_of_he_spinel_oxide"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A solventless thermolysis route can synthesize the seven-metal high-entropy spinel oxide.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC12005821::web::007::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Optimized thermolysis conditions will produce a uniform spinel phase with high configurational disorder.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC12005821::web::007::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pt will be deposited on the high-entropy spinel at controlled sub-monolayer coverage.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conventional automotive exhaust catalysts typically consist of Pt supported on alumina.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conventional Pt/alumina automotive catalysts use higher Pt loadings than the proposed catalyst.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing configurational disorder in the seven-metal spinel improves CO oxidation performance.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Configurational disorder in the spinel increases oxygen mobility and promotes rapid oxygen exchange.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The disordered spinel creates stronger Pt-support interactions.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Strong Pt-support interactions disperse and stabilize Pt nanoparticles on the spinel.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stabilized Pt dispersion suppresses Pt sintering and catalyst deactivation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed Pt/high-entropy-spinel catalyst will accelerate oxidation reactions such as CO oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed catalyst will require substantially less Pt than conventional Pt/alumina.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed catalyst will have significantly lower light-off temperatures than conventional Pt/alumina under similar conditions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed catalyst will be more durable than conventional Pt/alumina during prolonged cycling.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The activity and durability benefits should hold during simulated automotive-exhaust testing at 300–600 °C with typical exhaust-gas mixtures.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
